From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] ld: pe-dll: filter the MSYS runtime from AArch64
 --export-all-symbols

On aarch64-pc-cygwin the DLL startup code comes from libmsys-2.0.a
(dll_entry.o: _msys_dll_entry, _msys_crt0_common, msys_attach_dll, ...),
but the export filters only know the Cygwin names and libcygwin.  Every DLL
linked with automatic exports therefore exported _msys_dll_entry, and a DLL
linked later against its import library resolved its own entry point
(-e _msys_dll_entry) to that import: its entry was the other DLL's startup
code, which registers the other DLL's data and bss ranges with the runtime.
fork() then never copies the borrowing DLL's data to the child; perl, for
one, whose interpreter DLL got its entry from msys-crypt-2.dll, crashed in
every forked child.

Add the MSYS names and libmsys-2.0, as MSYS2's native binutils does
(0100-binutils-2.37-msys2.patch).  The x86_64 DLLs export none of these
symbols; with this the aarch64 ones match them.

Signed-off-by: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
---
 ld/pe-dll.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ld/pe-dll.c b/ld/pe-dll.c
--- a/ld/pe-dll.c
+++ b/ld/pe-dll.c
@@ -218,6 +218,7 @@
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("_NULL_IMPORT_DESCRIPTOR") },
   /* Entry point symbols, and entry hooks.  */
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("cygwin_crt0") },
+  { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("msys_crt0") },
 #ifdef pe_use_plus
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("DllMain") },
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("DllEntryPoint") },
@@ -225,6 +226,10 @@
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("_cygwin_dll_entry") },
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("_cygwin_crt0_common") },
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("_cygwin_noncygwin_dll_entry") },
+  { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("_msys_dll_entry") },
+  { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("_msys_crt0_common") },
+  { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("_msys_nonmsys_dll_entry") },
+  { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("msys_attach_dll") },
 #else
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("DllMain@12") },
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("DllEntryPoint@0") },
@@ -233,6 +238,10 @@
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("_cygwin_crt0_common@8") },
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("_cygwin_noncygwin_dll_entry@12") },
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("cygwin_attach_dll") },
+  { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("_msys_dll_entry@12") },
+  { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("_msys_crt0_common@8") },
+  { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("_msys_nonmsys_dll_entry@12") },
+  { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("msys_attach_dll") },
 #endif
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("cygwin_premain0") },
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("cygwin_premain1") },
@@ -401,6 +410,7 @@
 {
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("libcegcc") },
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("libcygwin") },
+  { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("libmsys-2.0") },
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("libgcc") },
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("libgcc_s") },
   { STRING_COMMA_LEN ("libstdc++") },
